Sorry, I should have been clearer. This change is good, but the `afterWriteTickInfo` property should still be retained as a non-enumerable alias.

e.g.

```js
Object.defineProperty(this, 'afterWriteTickInfo', {
  enumerable: false,
  get() { return this[kAfterWriteTickInfo]; },
  set(val) { this[kAfterWriteTickInfo] = val; }
});
```

The alias can then be separated deprecated.
